commands.description:
Describe what is on screen as an indented tree, one element per line with a ref to pass to click, set_widget_value, press_keys and run_javascript (a page element's to mouse_gesture too): the widgets of every shown window, the rows of lists, trees and tables, each shown popup after the window it opened from, the main menus, the 3D canvas's toolbar items and gizmos, each ImGui panel drawn in the last frame with its items and text, and the elements of each shown web page (dialogs, the setup wizard, sign-in, plugin windows) under its web view. With a modal dialog open, only the topmost dialog's pages are read. Refs go stale when their element goes away: call list_widgets again then. Prefer run_action and the typed tools when one fits.
A locator names an element without a ref, in any session (export_replay records them); index (0-based) picks one of several matches:
- a widget: {label, class, name, within, index}, within being its window's title; a notebook page: {tab: "General", within}
- a setting's field: {option: "layer_height"}
- {menu: "File>Export>Export G-code"}, {gltoolbar: "arrange"}, {gizmo: "Move"}
- an ImGui item: {imgui: "label", imgui_name?: "name", window?, canvas?, index?}, by its label, its name or both
- a row of a list, tree, table or drop-down list: {row: "Plate 1>Cube>Cylinder", column?, within?, index?}, by its last labels; column names the cell to act on
- a plate or one of its icons in the Prepare view: {plate_icon: "lock", plate: 0}, the icon being plate, delete, orient, arrange, lock, settings, name, move_to_front, filament_map or imex_mode
- a web page's element: {web: "Next", kind?: "button", css?: "#AcceptBtn", within?, index?}, by the label list_widgets lists (exactly, else ignoring case, else a part of it), its kind, a CSS selector (the id a line shows as name: name=#save is {css: "#save"}), or together. Without within it looks in the topmost dialog's pages while one is open, else in every shown page, and it waits up to 3 s for its element.
